id: pm-jev-tokenizer-admission
title: Refuse local decisions that exceed digest-bound tokenizer context
description: "Add exact rendered decision prompt admission bound to an immutable local model digest, preserving all typed questions and options."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: admission,decision,"gh:unbraind/pm-jev#92",tokenizer
created_at: "2026-11-05T04:39:51.590Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T15:07:14.178Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Long multibyte state passing byte heuristics refuses before inference when it exceeds the pinned model context; valid short typed batches retain every option and question; one receipt identifies the smallest token reduction needed.
comments[33]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-05T04:40:17.822Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current pm-jev main, host SDK and pm-context/pm-rl/pm-rlm: current code has UTF-8 budgets, decision capability discovery, calibrated digest checks and usage accounting; host output token budgets describe emitted context. None admits actual model-template-question input fit. This feature belongs at runDecision before local inference. No import/export/sync, journal, mutation, status-role or shared persistent state is added; those generic contracts remain delegated to existing SDK paths."
  "2026-11-05T04:54:50.735Z",codex-agent,"Implemented strict shared batch admission, the typed SDK receipt/refusals and jev admit. Both metadata and inference use a full sha256 model reference after one alias resolution. Initial supported profile pins the published Tev1 systemone template and reconstructs the native qwen35 BPE tokenizer from model metadata, including every question and option. Read-only no-git public acceptance: 26 tracker items read, 8 samples, 24 questions and 56 options retained; prompt maxima 158..298 tokens; receipts at most 484 bytes. Native usage independently matched 210 counted tokens. A 35,450-byte multibyte stress document counted 14,125 tokens against num_ctx 8,192 and refused with an exact 5,934-token deficit before inference. Tracker hashes stayed unchanged; details in docs/decision-admission-evidence.json."
  "2026-11-05T04:56:43.550Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding measurement comment: the stress input is exactly 35,282 bytes (the committed evidence is authoritative). All other recorded token counts, limits and deficits are unchanged. Production audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Local typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication passed; strict refusal and replay property tests are still being completed."
  "2026-11-05T05:01:42.276Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, only runDecision admission was bypassed. The exact-multibyte regression failed with Missing expected rejection (0 passed, 1 failed); the implementation checkout was never changed. The fixed implementation passes that regression. Alias-retarget interleavings at tags, show and SDK retry boundaries all keep the originally admitted digest. No shared durable admission state or mutation/compensation path exists. The 500-sequence SDK read-back property passed, including older-state replays, Unicode and CRLF variants and all projected native fields."
  "2026-11-05T05:05:03.355Z",codex-agent,"Validation complete locally: 9 admission tests passed including 500 seeded SDK replay/edit sequences; 8 focused admission regressions passed through pm test --run --progress (tracking is disabled, so this comment records the result); 26 existing decision/transport tests passed. The three new source modules measure 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines under targeted c8. Typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero-duplication and production audit pass. Packed acceptance passed all five modes (project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx), with JSON and TOON admission in every mode, and packed SDK checks: archive sha512 14b022d1c67a6889032777b7efcf4c87684daa87cb37c782d767ca84b07c2bd98685d09bc3afde80c32c488ac4244b3974fc7a25b61d521ceac06aec3baaf3aa. Full npm and Bun release gates will run on CI at the final commit; final run URLs/counts belong in the PR evidence. No merge or release is authorized. Initial profile scope: exact Tev1 systemone plus qwen35 BPE, safe-integer JSON, digest-addressable native Ollama; unsupported profiles fail closed."
  "2026-11-05T05:18:52.694Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility follow-up: local inference correctly reports the immutable digest, so the live assertion now checks the installed digest. The replay adapter also pins its captured model digest across calls and accepts native digest responses while retaining legacy alias-response compatibility. A retargeted alias cannot change an existing replay adapter. Both replay files pass (10 tests), including through pm test --run --progress --only-last. Reverting only the replay response guard in a disposable copy fails the native-digest case (agreement 0 instead of 3); the fixed regression passes. Live local triage, dedupe, ask and all four positive/negative/safety gate cases passed in one synthetic no-mutation scenario (161 seconds). Additional native count parity matched choice 148/148, score 130/130, structured instructions 141/141 and structured criteria 140/140. The original CI matrix remains queued with zero executed gates; the final head will receive fresh CI and another five-mode packed acceptance."
  "2026-11-05T05:32:11.037Z",codex-agent,"Final native parity audit found and fixed a whitespace edge: JavaScript trim discarded Unicode blanks that the pinned native template keeps. Native measurements were 111 counted versus 117 actual tokens for a non-breaking-space/form-feed case; the corrected six-ASCII-whitespace fallback now counts exactly 117. Separate native checks confirm literal non-breaking spaces and BOMs and ASCII form-feed/vertical-tab fallback. The new byte-BPE equivalence regression passes and fails when only description fallback is reverted in a disposable copy (447 versus 566 tokens). The whitespace regression also passed through pm test --run --progress --only-last. Static checks pass; final focused coverage and five-mode packed acceptance are recorded in the PR. CI remains pending; follow-up source changes require a fresh exact-head run. The original 30-minute CI waiting cutoff is retained."
  "2026-11-05T05:40:32.465Z",codex-agent,"CI integration follow-up: superseded run 41973261751 reported 399/417 tests passing and 18 failures. The common causes were the scripted fixture model missing from admission inventory and the existing dedupe producer emitting fractional rank metadata into the integer-only model-state domain. The producer now emits that rank as display text while public candidate scores, option identities, order and numeric ranking remain unchanged. All 57 agent-UX/dedupe/evaluation tests covering those failures now pass. The full admission file passes 11 tests including the 500-sequence SDK read-back property; static checks also pass. A producer-only behavioral revert fails the new admission regression; the fixed producer succeeds. The producer regression passed through pm test --run --progress --only-last. The 30-minute CI waiting cutoff has elapsed: fresh final-head gate URLs/counts and the final packed artifact result will be recorded on the PR, with no full-gate success claim until actual completion."
  "2026-11-05T07:30:39.287Z",codex-agent,"Review round on bd747d2: fetched all three unresolved threads and every comment (no pagination remaining); latest CodeRabbit review contains no outside-diff findings. Verified option compatibility, untagged discovery, and repeated tokenizer construction. Plan: preserve existing producer/parser domains, align native option labels with upstream protocol, normalize installed names, and cache only validated endpoint-scoped full-digest profiles with a bounded LRU. Add behavioral revert proofs and run unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Remote head is current and contains main."
  "2026-11-05T07:36:08.756Z",codex-agent,"Verified producer bounds: dedupe accepts 32 candidates and adds none (33 options); triage emits configured types plus keep-current; parseQuestionsDocument accepts 255 choice labels. Native pplx-decider enumerates A..Z then AA..ZZ, retaining single-token codes up to 255 (upstream tools/server/server-decision.cpp). Admission accepts that existing domain, derives native labels, and refuses insufficient capacity with option_limit_exceeded and a model/question/dedupe/registry remedy. Self-review found the same untagged-name defect in calibration, replay and doctor; they now share one normalizer that distinguishes registry ports from tags. Profiles use an endpoint-scoped full-digest eight-entry LRU; aliases resolve each time and replay remains creation-time pinned. Metadata-changing fixtures now use distinct digests for distinct immutable profiles."
  "2026-11-05T07:39:10.606Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in disposable copies (production checkout unchanged; tests import source): eight isolated mutations each produced 0 passes / 1 failure: option cap 255 to 24, native label selection to ASCII offset, admission name matching to exact equality, calibration name matching to exact equality, replay name matching to exact equality, doctor name matching to exact equality, cache-hit bypass, and cache key with digest removed. The first label oracle allowed a mutation because both wrong and correct labels occupy one token; a contextual punctuation merge now independently exposes the wrong rendered label and the mutation fails. Fixed five-test review suite passed through pinned pm test --run --progress --only-last. Tracker test-result tracking is disabled, so results and proofs are recorded here. Existing admission tests (including 500 SDK edit/replay sequences) and replay tests passed; two early review-test fixture assumptions were corrected (structured-clone prototypes and replay model-name allowlist)."
  "2026-11-05T07:55:15.831Z",codex-agent,"First full npm gate: all 424 tests passed, but the unchanged branch threshold failed at 99.97 percent. Coverage isolated one existing missing branch: translateDecisionError admission-refusal mapping in index.ts. Added an end-to-end runDecision refusal assertion that verifies the stable code and remedy; added normalized legacy replay-response coverage and the native score allow/refuse boundary (10/11). Native Tev1 parser explicitly limits scores to 2..10, so that existing bound is correct despite the open-ended SDK tuple. Focused five-test suite, lint and zero-duplication gates pass. Re-running complete npm and Bun gates under isolated Git identity; no thresholds, source scope, or gate commands were changed."
  "2026-11-05T08:08:18.119Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check PASSED under isolated HOME, disabled system/global Git config, and credential-free npm configuration: 424 tests passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped; all 46 inventoried source files covered at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (7979 statement/line counters, 402 functions, 3838 branches). Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, build, release identity, docstrings, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog check and publish-attestation checks passed. The initial 99.97 percent failure was real missing regression coverage, fixed with an end-to-end admission refusal assertion; it was not a timeout. Ten disposable behavioral reverts each fail 0 passed / 1 failed: option cap; native label selection; admission, calibration, replay and doctor inventory name matching; normalized legacy replay response; admission-refusal translation; cache-hit bypass; digest omitted from cache key. Restored implementations pass all five review tests. Bun full gate is running serially at unchanged thresholds; no code changes remain planned."
  "2026-11-05T08:16:57.786Z",codex-agent,"Final review validation: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check both PASS under isolated Git identity and credential-free npm configuration. Each full suite: 424 passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped; coverage across the unchanged 46-file source scope is 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, including 7979 statement/line counters, 402 functions and 3838 branches. Production audit is clean, duplication remains zero, and both pack dry-runs include 180 files with identical package shasum. Final five review tests also passed through pinned pm test --run --progress --only-last; automatic test-result tracking remains disabled, so this comment preserves the receipt. Threads PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z8SfW, PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z8Sfa and PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z8Sfk are all fixed; no outside-diff findings or invalid findings were present. Ten behavioral reverts fail and restored tests pass. Rebuilt committed dist output is included. No runtime timeouts needed retry. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress. Fresh final-head CI will appear at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/92/checks after push; CI is a separate pending claim. No thread replies/resolution, merge, release, or unrelated issue filing."
  "2026-11-05T08:58:30.479Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: fetched all review threads and every comment (no pagination omissions). Valid unresolved docs threads PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z-2iD and PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z-2iP; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Remote head d2cb8d8 already contains origin/main. Plan: installed-package npx/bunx examples verified against one packed archive, refusal mapping table checked against declared codes and actual API/host outcomes, whole-PR documentation audit, behavioral doc reverts in disposable copies, unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-11-05T09:04:56.488Z",codex-agent,"Implemented installed-package paths for npx and native bunx in the guide; whole-PR self-review found matching README, CLI help and missing-file remedy examples and aligned them. No inference behavior changed. The refusal table covers all six declared codes, distinguishes the reserved context_exceeded code from negative overflow receipts, and checks real direct refusals plus host code/exit/receipt/remedy mapping. Packed-install regression executes the guide commands verbatim and validates JSON/TOON parity, no inference, unchanged no-git tracker, CLI invalid-input exit 2 and overflow exit 1."
  "2026-11-05T09:07:42.224Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs in a disposable copy: replacing only installed batch paths with examples/decision-admission.json makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/admission-docs-install.test.ts fail (exit 1): the real installed host returns invalid_input, exit_code 2 before inference. Reverting the refusal documentation to the previous guide makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/admission-docs.test.ts fail (exit 1): its documented code set is empty instead of the six actual declared refusal codes. Both fixes were restored in finally; restoration is being rechecked. Linked pm tests: all six linked commands passed; result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so results are preserved here. Duplication remains 0 percent and lint passes."
  "2026-11-05T09:19:03.921Z",codex-agent,"Restoration proof completed: both documentation regressions pass after restoring the fixes (2 passed / 0 failed). Full npm run release:check PASSED with isolated HOME, disabled system/global Git configuration and a credential-free child environment: 426 passed / 0 failed / 0 canceled / 0 skipped. Coverage: all 46 inventoried source files at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (7979 statement/line counters, 402 functions, 3843 branches). All release stages passed, including 0 percent duplication, 1120 documented declarations, production audit with zero vulnerabilities, 180-file pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation checks. All six linked pm commands passed (8 + 10 + 1 + 1 + 5 + 2 = 27 tests). Packed npx/bunx JSON/TOON examples passed with zero inference and no tracker changes. Bun full release gate is running serially next; no timeouts or retries so far."
  "2026-11-05T09:25:20.209Z",codex-agent,"Full bun run release:check also PASSED under isolated HOME, disabled system/global Git configuration and a credential-free child environment: 426 passed / 0 failed / 0 canceled / 0 skipped; all 46 source files at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (7979 statement/line counters, 402 functions, 3843 branches). All static, identity, docstring, 0 percent duplication, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), 180-file pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. npm and Bun packed-guide tests used identical SHA-512-checked archive bytes. No local timeout failures or retries occurred. Both valid unresolved threads PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z-2iD and PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6z-2iP are fixed with recorded failing reverts and passing restoration; README/help/missing-file guidance self-review instances are covered by the packed test. Committed dist was rebuilt. No new pm CLI/SDK defects found. Final source and tracker evidence will be pushed together; fresh exact-head CI remains a separate pending claim at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/92/checks. No replies, thread resolutions, mentions, merge or release. Claim released next; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-05T09:39:24.719Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3 on 042e387: all review threads and all unresolved comments fetched with no remaining pagination. One valid thread PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs60ANpF; latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings. Remote head is current and contains main. Confirmed surrogate splitting at the 4000-unit text and 128-unit tag bounds. Whole-repository slice audit also found pairState title/text, exemplar body packing, and redacted diagnostic truncation. Plan: one shared UTF-16 boundary helper, unchanged strict admission validation and existing budgets/markers, deterministic boundary and seeded astral fuzz regressions, isolated behavioral reverts, rebuilt dist, unchanged full npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-11-05T09:44:27.909Z",codex-agent,"Implemented boundedText shared by state text, both tag projections, pair title/text, both exemplar cuts and diagnostic redaction. Existing 4000/128/320/1600/500 UTF-16 limits and truncation markers are preserved; strict surrogate validation is unchanged and malformed source strings remain refused. Seven focused tests pass, including 128 seeded mixed-astral fuzz sequences with independent code-point prefix oracles, exact/straddling boundaries, non-git tracker read-back through local decision admission, and malformed-input refusal. The linked test passed through pm test --run --progress --only-last (7 passed, 0 failed); project test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment preserves results. Build-test, lint, docstrings (47 source files, 1122 declarations), and zero duplication pass. Initial test fixture assumptions (tags option shape and exemplar byte overhead) were corrected; no product or SDK defect was involved. Remaining slices are arrays, ASCII protocol prefixes, exact whole-description removal, or private lexical trigram windows; no other emitted text truncation remains."
  "2026-11-05T09:44:42.467Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed in a disposable source copy; the package worktree was never mutated. Each isolated reversion failed with an assertion (0 passed, 1 failed, exit 1): boundedText return bypass; truncateStateText raw slice; projectItemState tag raw slice; projectTriageState tag raw slice; pairState title raw slice; pairState text raw slice; budgetedBody initial raw slice; budgetedBody halved raw slice; redactedSourceLine raw slice. Exact test form: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=<pattern> test/bounded-text.test.ts; patterns respectively: bounded text retains; item and triage projection (three mutations); pair evidence keeps (two); exemplar packing keeps (two); diagnostic text respects. Every copy mutation was restored in finally; all seven tests then passed (0 failed/canceled/skipped). The first pair-text mutation attempt was syntactically invalid and was discarded as non-evidence, then rerun as a valid behavioral revert. Full npm and Bun release gates run serially next at unchanged thresholds under isolated Git identity and credential-free child environments."
  "2026-11-05T09:57:05.091Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check PASSED with isolated HOME, disabled global/system Git configuration, and credential-free child environment: 433 tests passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped; all 47 inventoried source files at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, build, release identity, docstrings (1122 declarations), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation checks all passed. No timeout or retry was needed. The new boundary/fuzz/non-git suite contributed seven passing tests; nine isolated valid behavioral reverts each failed its targeted regression and restoration passed all seven. The unchanged Bun full gate runs next, serially."
  "2026-11-05T10:10:17.672Z",codex-agent,"Final round 3 validation: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check both PASS under isolated Git identity and credential-free child environments. Each full suite: 433 passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped. Coverage totals match exactly: all 47 inventoried source files at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines; 7988 statement/line counters, 403 functions, 3849 branches. All static/build/identity/docstring/zero-duplication/prod-audit/changelog/publish-attestation stages passed; production audit has zero vulnerabilities. Both 184-file package dry-runs have shasum f017e5d06a8225eeca30b25e4fea374ce1469070. No timeout or retry was needed. Valid thread PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs60ANpF is fixed with the state and both tag projections covered; self-review fixes pair title/text, initial/halved exemplar cuts and diagnostics. Nine valid isolated behavioral reverts each fail with an assertion; restored seven-test suite passes. Source, new regression, rebuilt committed dist and append-only tracker evidence are committed together. Claim is released next; item stays in progress for orchestrator verification. Fresh pushed-head CI/re-review is a separate pending claim at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/92/checks. No new pm CLI/SDK bugs found; linked test-result tracking is disabled and receipts are preserved in comments. No thread reply/resolution, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-11-05T13:30:54.325Z",codex-agent,"Round 4: fetched all unresolved review threads and all their comments (3 threads, no pagination gaps), plus latest review body (Windows runner finding). Verified offline-install, optional Bun, and duplicate score-encoding calibration defects. Merged current main first; resolving each with behavioral regression evidence. No review replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-05T13:37:39.008Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 fixes: standard packed guide smoke unpacks the local archive beside the existing lockfile dependencies, with an empty cache, offline npm and an unreachable registry. Node cases always run; absent Bun emits a diagnostic and a skipped subtest, with a separate Node-only PATH regression. Outside-diff Windows finding: npm/npx launch their installed JavaScript CLIs through Node, avoiding .cmd execution and shell quoting; synthetic Windows layout preserves spaced and literal shell-character arguments. duplicate_of fingerprint now includes candidate-score-string/1 so legacy numeric-score fits stay readable but cannot apply; current refits remain exchangeable across candidate identities. Whole PR source diff checked for the same registry/runtime/calibration classes; explicit network acceptance suites remain separate."
  "2026-11-05T13:39:17.984Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 behavioral revert proof in a disposable source copy: removing state_encoding from questionFingerprint fails legacy-fit rejection (7 tests: 6 pass, 1 fail); restoring the old fresh npm install in the offline, empty-cache smoke fails dependency resolution before running commands (1 fail); forcing the Bun subtest despite absent Bun fails with spawn bunx ENOENT in the Node-only regression (2 tests: 1 pass, 1 fail); reverting npmInvocation to direct manager execution fails the synthetic Windows runner assertion (1 fail). Each mutation was restored in finally; the combined restored suite is rerun before gates. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/decision-calibration.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/admission-docs-install.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/admission-install-runner.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"package runners bypass\" test/admission-install-runner.test.ts. All four mutants exit 1 as expected. Pinned pm test --run --match test/decision-calibration.test.ts --progress completed successfully; test result storage remains disabled by existing tracker settings, so results are recorded here."
  "2026-11-05T14:05:16.021Z",codex-agent,"Full npm release:check passed with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config: 437 tests passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped; all 47 inventoried source files reached 100% lines/branches/functions, and c8 reported 7988/7988 statements and lines, 403/403 functions, 3850/3850 branches. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, build, release identity, docstrings, production audit, pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. No timeout retries. Full Bun release gate now runs serially against the same code and unchanged thresholds. Restored focused regression suite passed 11/11; pinned pm linked run passed too."
  "2026-11-05T14:16:48.432Z",codex-agent,"Additional self-review: npm/npx runner lookup now follows POSIX executable symlinks as well as Windows and prefix layouts. The literal-argument fixture covers both layouts with a minimal child environment. Focused portability regression, test typecheck, lint and zero duplication pass. A tracker-only main sync was merged before final validation. Earlier npm full gate passed 437/437; the earlier Bun run was stopped because this test-helper addition requires fresh final-tree gate evidence. Both full gates will rerun serially without threshold changes."
  "2026-11-05T14:17:23.090Z",codex-agent,"Additional revert proof: removing only the POSIX symlink fallback from npmInvocation in a disposable copy fails the Windows/POSIX literal-argument fixture (1 test, 1 failure: Cannot locate the installed npm JavaScript entry point). Restoring the helper passes 1/1. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"package runners bypass\" test/admission-install-runner.test.ts. Five behavioral mutants now fail as expected; original four findings retain their recorded proofs."
  "2026-11-05T14:47:20.719Z",codex-agent,"Final-tree npm release:check passed after the POSIX fallback addition and latest tracker-only main merge: 437 passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped. All 47 inventoried source files meet unchanged 100% gates; c8 totals are 7988 lines/statements, 403 functions, 3850 branches, all covered. Audit reports zero vulnerabilities and pack dry-run lists 184 files. No timeout retries. Final-tree Bun release:check is now running serially; no further code or test changes are planned."
  "2026-11-05T14:48:46.759Z",codex-agent,"Counter correction for the final-tree npm run: reading its c8 JSON summary confirms 3849/3849 covered branches, not 3850/3850. The earlier pre-portability run reported 3850; the final run retains 7988/7988 lines and statements and 403/403 functions. Every dimension remains 100%, the source inventory remains 47 files, and the suite result remains 437/437 with no failures, cancellations or skips."
  "2026-11-05T15:07:11.535Z",codex-agent,"Final validation complete: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 437 tests, with 0 failures, cancellations or skips. Both use isolated HOME, disabled global/system Git config and credential-free npm configuration, run serially with at most 2 test workers, retain unchanged 100% thresholds and report all 47 inventoried source files covered. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, build, release identity, 1122 documented declarations, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), 184-file pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. All five behavioral revert mutants fail and restored focused tests pass (11/11 combined, plus 1/1 expanded portability fixture). No timeout retries. dist is rebuilt. Native Windows execution was unavailable; the deterministic Windows/POSIX runner fixture covers invocation and literal arguments. CI will be checked after pushing; thread replies/resolutions, merging and releases remain out of scope."
